DTSTAMP:20260711T000000Z
SUMMARY:Painting with Tea: America 250 Edition
DESCRIPTION:with Smriti Sangal\, Culture Chauraha \n\nImmerse yourself in a 
 sensory art experience where brewed tea becomes your paint and history 
 becomes your inspiration. In this aromatic workshop\, participants will 
 create sepia-toned artworks using tea washes\, exploring warm gradients\, 
 soft textures\, and the natural stain of tea. Surrounded by the calming 
 scent of brewed tea\, you'll experiment with brush techniques to build 
 depth\, contrast\, and detail.\n\nUsing references inspired by the Boston 
 Tea Party among other general motifs\, you'll design expressive pieces 
 featuring ships\, slogans\, and freedom-themed imagery--or create your own 
 playful\, modern interpretations. This workshop blends creativity with 
 storytelling\, offering a relaxing hands-on experience suited for all skill 
 levels.\n\nParticipants leave with a beautiful tea-painted artwork and a 
 newfound appreciation for this unique medium.\n\nThis workshop is designed 
 for adults. All materials provided.\nRegistration is required.\n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Craft
UID:LibCal-10341-16702349
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16702349
