BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260828T150000Z
DTEND:20260828T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260828T000000Z
SUMMARY:August Book Club: The Art of Losing
DESCRIPTION:A book club for adults who want to read in community. We meet 
 one Friday morning a month to chat about a title we read in 
 common.\n\n--\nSummer World Literature Series\n\nTHE ART OF LOSING \nby 
 Alice Zeniter (France)\ntranslated by Frank Wynne\n\nNaïma's family comes 
 from Algeria\, but she knows it only from what she experiences in her 
 grandparents' tiny apartment in Normandy: the food her grandmother cooks\, 
 the precious things they carried when they fled. Naïma's father claims to 
 remember nothing\, has made himself French. But now\, one of them is going 
 back and Naïma will see for herself what was left behind\, including the 
 family secrets. A powerful\, moving family novel that spans three 
 generations\, across seventy years and two shores of the Mediterranean Sea. 
 \n\n** Participating in the World Championship Challenge? Read this book as 
 your Group A pick\, and let us know how it fares in your tournament 
 bracket! **\n\nCopies available at the Circulation Desk starting July 
 24.\n\n
LOCATION:Literacy Room\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10341-16592775
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/westorange/artoflosing
END:VEVENT
